# Pinned opam repository commits. Read by `make deps` (via pin-opam-repos) and by
# .github/actions/setup-hazel-toolchain, so CI and local development install from
# the same repository state.
#
# hazel.opam.locked pins which package *versions* the solver picks; it cannot pin
# their *metadata*. opam has no content hashes and upstream edits published
# versions in place, which can make a pinned version uninstallable with no change
# on our side. See issue #2334, and ocaml/opam-repository#10531 for why this is a
# standing property rather than a one-off.
#
# Moved forward by `make change-deps` alongside the regenerated lock file, so the
# two always describe the same repository state.
#
# OPAM_REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE_SHA goes away with issue #1707.
OPAM_REPOSITORY_SHA=9c0fb80b783c632ef0024ba0cc86df4ced6c19aa
OPAM_REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE_SHA=92f1a8075c3493fa8f4482b885993a91dceee07b
